{:edb/db-before-t 2763 :edb/db-after-t 2764 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536076 50 #inst "2026-10-09T14:27:23.297Z" 13194139536076 true] [17592186221355 1020 #edb/ref 17592186382530 13194139536076 true] [17592186221355 1020 #edb/ref 17592186382537 13194139536076 true] [17592186221356 1020 #edb/ref 17592186382544 13194139536076 true] [17592186221356 1020 #edb/ref 17592186382551 13194139536076 true] [17592186221356 1020 #edb/ref 17592186382558 13194139536076 true] [17592186382530 1017 #edb/ref 17592186382531 13194139536076 true] [17592186382530 1089 "q-335377" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382530 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536076 true] [17592186382530 1100 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)={x}^{2}(t)+3x(t)+y(t)+1 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-3x(t)-{y}^{2}(t)+2y(t)-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of ODEs above. An equilibrium point of the system is $[-1,\\,1]^{T}.$ Which of the following is the system obtained by shifting this equilibrium to the origin?" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382530 1113 #uuid "67ef18c6-5d45-520b-b960-5f958b495e82" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382530 1145 "To shift the system's equilibrium from ${x}^{∗}$ to the origin, we define the deviation vector\n\n$$\nu=x-{x}^{∗},\n$$\n\nwhere $x=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $u=[\\begin{aligned}u(t) \\\\ v(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nu=x-[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⇒\\,x=u+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,{x}^{′}={u}^{′}.\n$$\n\nIn coordinate form, this can be written as follows:\n\n$$\nx(t)=u(t)-1,\\,y(t)=v(t)+1,\\,{x}^{′}(t)={u}^{′}(t),\\,{v}^{′}(t)={y}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now substitute these into the given system.\n\n- Substituting into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & ={x}^{2}(t)+3x(t)+y(t)+1 \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =(u(t)-1)^{2}+3(u(t)-1)+(v(t)+1)+1 \\\\  & =({u}^{2}(t)-2u(t)+1)+3u(t)-3+v(t)+1+1 \\\\  & ={u}^{2}(t)+u(t)+v(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Substituting into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =-3x(t)-{y}^{2}(t)+2y(t)-4 \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) & =-3(u(t)-1)-(v(t)+1)^{2}+2(v(t)+1)-4 \\\\  & =-3u(t)+3-({v}^{2}(t)+2v(t)+1)+2v(t)+2-4 \\\\  & =-3u(t)-{v}^{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the shifted system is the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)+u(t)+v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=-3u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382531 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382532 13194139536076 true] [17592186382531 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382533 13194139536076 true] [17592186382531 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382534 13194139536076 true] [17592186382531 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382535 13194139536076 true] [17592186382531 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382536 13194139536076 true] [17592186382531 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536076 true] [17592186382531 1041 "selection" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382531 1104 #edb/ref 17592186382535 13194139536076 true] [17592186382531 1110 #uuid "f6d81a5e-5920-5bb5-a87d-a682ea9af8c8" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382532 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)+u(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=-3u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)+v(t)\\end{aligned}" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382532 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536076 true] [17592186382532 1111 #uuid "5830ab83-4536-518d-9ee2-3906d7f12d2b" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382533 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)+{v}^{2}(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=-3u(t)+v(t)\\end{aligned}" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382533 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536076 true] [17592186382533 1111 #uuid "fbf7d96f-5625-5a72-8c43-cc611a413676" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382534 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=2{u}^{2}(t)+u(t)+v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382534 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536076 true] [17592186382534 1111 #uuid "86822d51-08a3-5414-b2fb-65f2ef3af1be" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382535 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)+u(t)+v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=-3u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382535 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536076 true] [17592186382535 1111 #uuid "e3376030-8837-55f9-948f-0ff849889be8" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382536 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)+u(t)+{v}^{2}(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=-u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382536 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536076 true] [17592186382536 1111 #uuid "0b771851-2d66-5637-aed2-ba61f79f9680" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382537 1017 #edb/ref 17592186382538 13194139536076 true] [17592186382537 1089 "q-335380" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382537 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536076 true] [17592186382537 1100 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)={x}^{2}(t)+{y}^{2}(t)-3x(t)-y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=2x(t)-{y}^{2}(t)+5y(t)-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of ODEs above. An equilibrium point of the system is $[1,\\,2]^{T}.$ Which of the following is the system obtained by shifting this equilibrium to the origin?" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382537 1113 #uuid "a6291bca-1fab-53ea-a875-cc77eae942da" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382537 1145 "To shift the system's equilibrium from ${x}^{∗}$ to the origin, we define the deviation vector\n\n$$\nu=x-{x}^{∗},\n$$\n\nwhere $x=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $u=[\\begin{aligned}u(t) \\\\ v(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nu=x-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,⇒\\,x=u+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,{x}^{′}={u}^{′}.\n$$\n\nIn coordinate form, this can be written as follows:\n\n$$\nx(t)=u(t)+1,\\,y(t)=v(t)+2,\\,{x}^{′}(t)={u}^{′}(t),\\,{v}^{′}(t)={y}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now substitute these into the given system.\n\n- Substituting into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & ={x}^{2}(t)+{y}^{2}(t)-3x(t)-y(t) \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =(u(t)+1)^{2}+(v(t)+2)^{2}-3(u(t)+1)-(v(t)+2) \\\\  & =({u}^{2}(t)+2u(t)+1)+({v}^{2}(t)+4v(t)+4)-3u(t)-3-v(t)-2 \\\\  & ={u}^{2}(t)-u(t)+{v}^{2}(t)+3v(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Substituting into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =2x(t)-{y}^{2}(t)+5y(t)-8 \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) & =2(u(t)+1)-(v(t)+2)^{2}+5(v(t)+2)-8 \\\\  & =2u(t)+2-({v}^{2}(t)+4v(t)+4)+5v(t)+10-8 \\\\  & =2u(t)+v(t)-{v}^{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the shifted system is the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)-u(t)+{v}^{2}(t)+3v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2u(t)+v(t)-{v}^{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382539 13194139536076 true] [17592186382538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382540 13194139536076 true] [17592186382538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382541 13194139536076 true] [17592186382538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382542 13194139536076 true] [17592186382538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382543 13194139536076 true] [17592186382538 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536076 true] [17592186382538 1041 "selection" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382538 1104 #edb/ref 17592186382541 13194139536076 true] [17592186382538 1110 #uuid "ac906d6e-9252-5102-a285-d574e59dd762" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382539 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)-u(t)+v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2{u}^{2}(t)+v(t)-{v}^{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382539 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536076 true] [17592186382539 1111 #uuid "30697ebe-2afa-5c29-8ac7-a4cbbf3dcad2" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382540 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=2{u}^{2}(t)-u(t)+{v}^{2}(t)+3v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382540 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536076 true] [17592186382540 1111 #uuid "2930cd30-1bb8-596f-a39b-2c8e9e036c92" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382541 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)-u(t)+{v}^{2}(t)+3v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2u(t)+v(t)-{v}^{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382541 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536076 true] [17592186382541 1111 #uuid "dd876892-fd02-54e5-8eaf-3f51b45b948b" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382542 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)-u(t)+{v}^{2}(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2u(t)+v(t)-3{v}^{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382542 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536076 true] [17592186382542 1111 #uuid "43da4ee8-a24d-53c6-a82a-c66d6f3f0b4d" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382543 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)+{v}^{2}(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2u(t)+v(t)\\end{aligned}" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382543 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536076 true] [17592186382543 1111 #uuid "c2c89baf-dc51-55da-a0ed-800398f60484" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382544 1017 #edb/ref 17592186382545 13194139536076 true] [17592186382544 1089 "q-335484" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382544 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536076 true] [17592186382544 1100 "A linear system of ODEs has the equilibrium at ${x}^{∗}=[2,\\,3]^{T}.$ Two linearly independent eigenvectors of the system's matrix are ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2}.$ After shifting using $u=x-{x}^{∗},$ the system becomes ${u}^{′}=Bu.$ Which of the following is **guaranteed** to be an eigenvector of the matrix $B?$" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382544 1113 #uuid "8027b2a7-781d-5bbf-89b4-b685be3303c9" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382544 1145 "After shifting a linear system, the eigenvalues and the corresponding eigenvectors remain unchanged.\n\nThus, the matrix $B$ in the shifted system has the same eigenvectors as the system's matrix in the original coordinates. These eigenvectors are ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2},$ or any nonzero vectors that are parallel to them.\n\nAmong the given options, the only vector that is nonzero and is guaranteed to be parallel to either ${w}_{1}$ or ${w}_{2}$ is the vector $5{w}_{1}.$" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382545 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382546 13194139536076 true] [17592186382545 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382547 13194139536076 true] [17592186382545 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382548 13194139536076 true] [17592186382545 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382549 13194139536076 true] [17592186382545 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382550 13194139536076 true] [17592186382545 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536076 true] [17592186382545 1041 "selection" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382545 1104 #edb/ref 17592186382547 13194139536076 true] [17592186382545 1110 #uuid "617d1b37-248a-582a-ab0c-2e6a110238e8" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382546 1034 "{w}_{2}-{x}^{∗}" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382546 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536076 true] [17592186382546 1111 #uuid "5f758aa4-8093-5259-b9f8-c2fe57294638" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382547 1034 "5{w}_{1}" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382547 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536076 true] [17592186382547 1111 #uuid "cd72f633-253a-5a6c-b1d1-b80eaaf8a938" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382548 1034 "0" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382548 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536076 true] [17592186382548 1111 #uuid "5c3e92c5-0226-51a9-a45f-762a4ec9fd95" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382549 1034 "{w}_{1}+{x}^{∗}" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382549 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536076 true] [17592186382549 1111 #uuid "dc51427f-7c45-5b35-8884-d8ed02848ea2" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382550 1034 "{x}^{∗}" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382550 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536076 true] [17592186382550 1111 #uuid "ce2a422e-6000-5c61-ae9c-bc9f48b43c65" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382551 1017 #edb/ref 17592186382552 13194139536076 true] [17592186382551 1089 "q-335488" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382551 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536076 true] [17592186382551 1100 "A linear system of ODEs has an equilibrium at ${x}^{∗}.$ One of the nullclines of the system has the equation $y=-4x+1$ in the corresponding phase space. The system is then shifted using $u=x-{x}^{∗}.$ Which of the following is **guaranteed** to be a nullcline of the shifted system?" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382551 1113 #uuid "6d7f5c3c-3dd8-541e-aac4-0b9cacaa8d19" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382551 1145 "After shifting a system, the geometric structure of the vector field is preserved. In particular, each nullcline is translated but retains its orientation, meaning its slope does not change.\n\nBecause the equilibrium is moved to the origin by the shift, the translated nullclines must pass through the origin in the shifted coordinates.\n\nThus, the nullclines of the shifted system pass through the origin and have the same slopes as the corresponding nullclines of the original system.\n\nAmong the given options, the only line that satisfies the above conditions is $y=-4x.$" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382552 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382553 13194139536076 true] [17592186382552 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382554 13194139536076 true] [17592186382552 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382555 13194139536076 true] [17592186382552 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382556 13194139536076 true] [17592186382552 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382557 13194139536076 true] [17592186382552 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536076 true] [17592186382552 1041 "selection" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382552 1104 #edb/ref 17592186382556 13194139536076 true] [17592186382552 1110 #uuid "213f80d0-d4db-5f3c-9afe-0cc9861f9dc5" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382553 1034 "y=4x" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382553 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536076 true] [17592186382553 1111 #uuid "34e7b2e2-7a71-56c3-a40c-910ff5b33f80" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382554 1034 "y=x-4" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382554 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536076 true] [17592186382554 1111 #uuid "e81ea147-132c-5167-b69b-6c1b94ccad60" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382555 1034 "y=-4x+1" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382555 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536076 true] [17592186382555 1111 #uuid "fb2f8738-ef9c-5fbb-9ca3-3e4c609d4f99" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382556 1034 "y=-4x" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382556 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536076 true] [17592186382556 1111 #uuid "68395084-33b8-52ab-b604-df5add6ccc41" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382557 1034 "y=-x" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382557 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536076 true] [17592186382557 1111 #uuid "319bfb5c-df15-5bf6-b7da-ea28dbada0e5" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382558 1017 #edb/ref 17592186382559 13194139536076 true] [17592186382558 1089 "q-335515" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382558 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536076 true] [17592186382558 1100 "A system of ODEs has an unstable saddle point at ${x}^{∗}.$ The system is then shifted using $u=x-{x}^{∗}.$ Which of the following best describes the point $(0,0)$ for the shifted system?" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382558 1113 #uuid "a43edc38-467a-59cb-be35-534236235f78" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382558 1145 "Shifting does not alter the local behavior near an equilibrium. So, the equilibrium retains its original classification (saddle, node, spiral, center, etc.).\n\nRecall that the shift moves the equilibrium to the origin.\n\nThus, the equilibrium at $(0,0)$ in the shifted system has the same classification as ${x}^{∗}$ in the original system.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"An unstable saddle point\"." 13194139536076 true] [17592186382559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382560 13194139536076 true] [17592186382559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382561 13194139536076 true] [17592186382559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382562 13194139536076 true] [17592186382559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382563 13194139536076 true] [17592186382559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382564 13194139536076 true] [17592186382559 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536076 true] [17592186382559 1041 "selection" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382559 1104 #edb/ref 17592186382561 13194139536076 true] [17592186382559 1110 #uuid "2aa542cd-2462-5f97-a5e9-feb37f93ef1d" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382560 1034 "An asymptotically stable spiral sink" 13194139536076 true] [17592186382560 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536076 true] [17592186382560 1111 #uuid "d66401ff-7ed9-5260-9758-2c7